# Testing

Backend tests use **JUnit 5**, **Mockito**, and Spring Boot **MockMvc**. Prefer slice tests over full `@SpringBootTest` unless a slice cannot prove the behavior.

## Stack

- **Unit:** JUnit 5 + Mockito (`@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)`). Mock ports (repositories, collaborators), not the class under test.
- **Web:** `@WebMvcTest` + `MockMvc` for controllers, status codes, and RFC 7807 bodies.
- **Persistence:** `@DataJpaTest` with **H2**. Do not point slice tests at PostgreSQL.
- **Frontend** (when present): colocate `*.test.ts(x)` / `*.spec.ts`. Do not re-test the HTTP contract MockMvc already covers.

## Style

- Names: `should_expectedBehavior_when_condition` or `@DisplayName`.
- Assert status, JSON path, and ProblemDetail `title` / `status` on errors.
- No `Thread.sleep`, no real network, no production secrets.

```java
// ❌ BAD
@Test void testCreate() { service.create(req); }

// ✅ GOOD
@WebMvcTest(TicketController.class)
class TicketControllerTest {
    @Autowired MockMvc mvc;
    @MockitoBean TicketService ticketService;

    @Test
    void should_return201_when_ticketCreated() throws Exception {
        // mock service, POST /api/v1/tickets, expect 201 + Location
    }
}
```

## State machine (parameterized)

Use **`@ParameterizedTest`** for legal and illegal ticket status transitions. One argument source for allowed transitions, one for rejected (expect domain exception / **422**). Do not copy a test per pair.

```java
@ParameterizedTest
@CsvSource({ "OPEN, IN_PROGRESS", "IN_PROGRESS, RESOLVED", "RESOLVED, CLOSED" })
void should_allow_transition(TicketStatus from, TicketStatus to) { ... }

@ParameterizedTest
@CsvSource({ "CLOSED, OPEN", "CANCELLED, IN_PROGRESS" })
void should_reject_illegal_transition(TicketStatus from, TicketStatus to) { ... }
```
